 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "standalone-info",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Appendix Table XXV — topic-encoder embedding sensitivity\n",
    "\n",
    "## Standalone reproduction\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook reproduces the seven-encoder embedding-sensitivity experiment for mixture sizes `K=2,...,6`. It does **not** depend on another TGCM notebook or on previously generated notebook outputs.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Environment\n",
    "\n",
    "- Python 3.12\n",
    "- PyTorch 2.6\n",
    "- NumPy 2.1\n",
    "- pandas 2.2\n",
    "- SciPy 1.15\n",
    "- scikit-learn 1.6\n",
    "- CUDA 11.8+ recommended for the full run; CPU is supported but slower.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Required evaluation assets\n",
    "\n",
    "Place these files either **next to this notebook** or under `tgcm_reproduction_support/data/assets/`:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. `synthetic_validation.tar.xz` — evaluation-only validation sequences for K=2 through K=6.\n",
    "2. `checkpoints_tgcm.tar.xz.part-000`\n",
    "3. `checkpoints_tgcm.tar.xz.part-001` — sanitized TGCM inference checkpoints for all seven embedding families and five seeds.\n",
    "\n",
    "No training corpus, optimizer state, API key, CAPture raw CSV archive, or other notebook output is required.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Evaluation contract\n",
    "\n",
    "The manuscript reports Macro-F1 as mean and sample standard deviation over five seeds. This notebook uses the paper's fixed-slot evaluation (`without_hungarian`); no permutation/Hungarian remapping is applied."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "standalone-bootstrap",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "import shutil\n",
    "import sys\n",
    "import urllib.request\n",
    "\n",
    "SUPPORT_REV = \"de9a81f726ebff439539edf345be98f619844fc8\"\n",
    "RAW_BASE = \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Irish-kw/TGCM_Website/\" + SUPPORT_REV + \"/reproduction\"\n",
    "NOTEBOOK_DIR = Path.cwd().resolve()\n",
    "\n",
    "def find_existing_root():\n",
    "    for candidate in (NOTEBOOK_DIR, *NOTEBOOK_DIR.parents):\n",
    "        if (candidate / \"tgcm_review\").is_dir() and (candidate / \"data\").is_dir():\n",
    "            return candidate\n",
    "    return None\n",
    "\n",
    "ROOT = find_existing_root()\n",
    "if ROOT is None:\n",
    "    ROOT = NOTEBOOK_DIR / \"tgcm_reproduction_support\"\n",
    "    files = [\n",
    "        'tgcm_review/__init__.py',\n",
    "        'tgcm_review/assets.py',\n",
    "        'tgcm_review/datasets.py',\n",
    "        'tgcm_review/metrics.py',\n",
    "        'tgcm_review/models.py',\n",
    "        'tgcm_review/inference.py',\n",
    "        'tgcm_review/paper_experiments.py',\n",
    "        'data/manifest.json',\n",
    "        'environment.yml',\n",
    "    ]\n",
    "    for relative in files:\n",
    "        destination = ROOT / relative\n",
    "        destination.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "        if not destination.exists():\n",
    "            print(f'Downloading support file: {relative}')\n",
    "            urllib.request.urlretrieve(f'{RAW_BASE}/{relative}', destination)\n",
    "\n",
    "asset_dir = ROOT / 'data' / 'assets'\n",
    "asset_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "required_assets = [\n",
    "    'synthetic_validation.tar.xz',\n",
    "    'checkpoints_tgcm.tar.xz.part-000',\n",
    "    'checkpoints_tgcm.tar.xz.part-001',\n",
    "]\n",
    "for filename in required_assets:\n",
    "    source = NOTEBOOK_DIR / filename\n",
    "    target = asset_dir / filename\n",
    "    if source.is_file() and not target.exists():\n",
    "        shutil.copy2(source, target)\n",
    "\n",
    "missing_assets = [name for name in required_assets if not (asset_dir / name).is_file()]\n",
    "if missing_assets:\n",
    "    print('\\nRequired evaluation asset files are missing:')\n",
    "    for name in missing_assets:\n",
    "        print('  -', name)\n",
    "    print('\\nPlace them next to this notebook or under:')\n",
    "    print(' ', asset_dir)\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print('All required evaluation assets are present.')\n",
    "\n",
    "if str(ROOT) not in sys.path:\n",
    "    sys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT))\n",
    "\n",
    "FULL_REPRODUCTION = True\n",
    "DEVICE = None  # None selects CUDA when available; use 'cpu' explicitly for CPU.\n",
    "MAX_SEQUENCES = None if FULL_REPRODUCTION else 512\n",
    "print(f'support_root={ROOT}')\n",
    "print('FULL PAPER RUN' if FULL_REPRODUCTION else 'SMOKE TEST — NOT A PAPER RESULT')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "run-embedding-sensitivity",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "if missing_assets:\n",
    "    raise FileNotFoundError(\n",
    "        'Missing required evaluation assets listed above. ' \
",
    "        'Place them next to the notebook and rerun this cell.'\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "from tgcm_review.paper_experiments import run_figure04\n",
    "\n",
    "detail, summary = run_figure04(\n",
    "    components=('tgcm',),\n",
    "    device=DEVICE,\n",
    "    max_sequences=MAX_SEQUENCES,\n",
    "    root=ROOT,\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "table25 = summary[\n",
    "    summary['alignment_scope'].eq('without_hungarian')\n",
    "    & summary['metric'].eq('Macro-F1')\n",
    "].copy()\n",
    "table25['Embedding'] = table25['model'].str.replace(r'^TGCM \\((.*)\\)$', r'\\1', regex=True)\n",
    "table25 = table25[['K', 'Embedding', 'mean', 'std']].sort_values(['K', 'Embedding']).reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "table25"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "paper-layout",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "paper_layout = (\n",
    "    table25.assign(value=table25.apply(lambda r: f\"{r['mean']:.3f} ± {r['std']:.3f}\", axis=1))\n",
    "    .pivot(index='K', columns='Embedding', values='value')\n",
    ")\n",
    "paper_layout"
   ]
  }
 ],
